        <exercise workspace="5in">
        <title>More on Inner Products</title>
       <statement>
        <p>
           There are some necessary properties an inner product must satisfy to make it a valid 
           inner product. For example, we must have that <m>\vvec \cdot \vvec \geq 0 </m>. But what makes a valid 
           definition a <q>good</q> definition?
        </p>
       </statement> 
       
